# These files run on Linux and are edited on Windows, so the line ending is
# not a preference.
#
# A shell script checked out with CRLF fails at its shebang -- the kernel looks
# for an interpreter called "bash\r", does not find one, and reports
#
#   bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#
# which reads as the *script* being missing rather than as a line ending. That
# is an hour of somebody's evening, at a customer site, over an invisible byte.
#
# Forced rather than left to whoever clones it: core.autocrlf is a setting on a
# machine, and the next machine is one nobody here configured.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.go   text eol=lf
go.mod text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
